feature: SLICE

requirements:
  - id: SLICE-1
    title: Slice Status
    description: >
      The slice CLI reports the current state of slice work: the active
      slice, the running Harvest timer, and the ticket's status. It is the
      read-back every other slice command and the orchestrator rely on.
    status: active                 # kept for current Spool; derived from items once extensions land
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-10-27
    rationale: >
      The one-timer rule and idempotent commands both depend on knowing the
      current state before acting. A read-only status command is the safest
      first piece and doubles as the orchestrator's read-back check.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - History or reporting of past slices
      - Slack focus status
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-1-1
        title: Nothing Active
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when status is run,
          then it reports no active slice and no running timer and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-1-2
        title: Active Slice
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T with a running timer for T,
          when status is run,
          then it reports ticket T, the slice id, the running timer,
          and the ticket's current status, and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-1-3
        title: State Mismatch
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a running Harvest timer whose ticket differs from the active
          slice's ticket, or a running timer with no active slice whether
          or not its notes name a ticket,
          when status is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-1-4
        title: Source Unavailable
        status: active
        description: >
          Given Harvest or the ticket system cannot be reached,
          when status is run,
          then it names the source that failed and exits non-zero,
          and does not report that source's state as empty.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-1-INV-1
        title: Status Is Read-Only
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run of status, in every starting state, Harvest, the
          ticket system, and local slice state are unchanged afterward.

  - id: SLICE-2
    title: Slice Open
    description: >
      Running slice open with a ticket number starts work on that ticket:
      a Harvest timer, an in-progress ticket, a branch and worktree, and a
      slice manifest, all checked against status before anything changes.
    status: active                 # kept for current Spool; derived from items once extensions land
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-10-27
    rationale: >
      Opening a slice is the entry point for every unit of work and exercises
      both integrations that matter most: Harvest timers and ticket updates.
      Making it deterministic means housekeeping never depends on the
      orchestrator remembering to do it. Harvest is tracked per ticket per
      day: every slice of ticket T on a given day logs to T's one entry for
      that day, the most recently updated entry dated today whose notes name
      T. A branch belongs to a feature, the ticket, and a slice is one step
      of it: every slice of T works on T's one branch and worktree. The
      branch is named <type>/<yyyymmdd>-<T>-<short title>, for example
      feature/20261102-TBOARD-405-dashboard: the type is chosen by the
      caller, who infers it from the ticket's content; the date is the day
      the branch is created; T stays uppercase so cu and mon can read the
      ticket from the branch; the short title is the ticket title lowercased
      with words joined by hyphens, cut to about 40 characters. T's branch is
      the one whose name has that shape with T after the date. Slice ids are
      internal to slice and never appear in Harvest notes, on tickets, or in
      branch names; commits made during a slice carry its id in their
      message, by convention rather than by anything slice enforces.
      Manifests are internal too, and live in slice's local state rather
      than in the worktree, so they cannot be committed by accident.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Pausing, resuming, or closing slices
      - Spec authoring and approval
      - Launching test or implementation agents
      - Choosing which ticket to work on
      - Inferring the branch type from the ticket; the caller passes it
      - Slack focus status
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-2-1
        title: Clean Open
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice, no running Harvest timer, and no Harvest
          entry for T today,
          when slice open is run with a valid ticket number T,
          then a new Harvest entry for T is running, noted with T and the
          ticket's title only, ticket T is in progress, a branch named from the --type given,
          today's date, T, and the ticket's title exists with its worktree,
          a slice manifest records T and the base commit,
          and the slice is active.

      - id: SLICE-2-2
        title: Stray Timer Running
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice and a Harvest timer running for ticket U
          or for no ticket,
          when slice open is run with ticket T,
          then the running timer is stopped before the timer for T starts,
          and the open otherwise completes as in SLICE-2-1.

      - id: SLICE-2-3
        title: Another Slice Active
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket U,
          when slice open is run with a different ticket T,
          then it fails, names the active slice for U,
          and changes nothing.

      - id: SLICE-2-4
        title: Same Slice Already Open
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T with its timer running,
          when slice open is run with ticket T,
          then it reports that the slice is already open, changes nothing,
          and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-2-5
        title: Unknown Ticket
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a ticket number that does not exist in the ticket system,
          when slice open is run with it,
          then it fails with an error naming the ticket and changes nothing.

      - id: SLICE-2-6
        title: Partial Failure
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a step of slice open fails after an earlier step succeeded,
          when slice open is run,
          then it undoes the earlier steps it performed in reverse order,
          including restarting any timer it stopped, deleting an entry only
          if this run created it, stopping an existing entry it restarted,
          and removing a branch or worktree only if this run created it,
          reports which step failed, and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-2-9
        title: Ticket Branch Exists
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice and exactly one existing branch for T, from
          an earlier slice, with or without its worktree,
          when slice open is run with T, and with no --type or the branch's
          own type,
          then the slice uses that branch, its worktree exists, creating it
          if missing, no other branch is created, the manifest's base commit
          is the branch's head, and the open otherwise completes as in
          SLICE-2-1.

      - id: SLICE-2-10
        title: Branch Options Conflict
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an existing branch for T,
          when slice open is run with T and --base, or with a --type other
          than the branch's type,
          then it fails, names the existing branch, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-2-11
        title: Type Required For New Branch
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no existing branch for T,
          when slice open is run with T and no --type,
          then it fails saying a type is needed to name the branch,
          changes nothing, and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-2-12
        title: Ambiguous Ticket Branch
        status: active
        description: >
          Given more than one existing branch for T,
          when slice open is run with T,
          then it fails, names every such branch, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-2-8
        title: Ticket Already Tracked Today
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice, no running Harvest timer, and a stopped
          Harvest entry for T dated today,
          when slice open is run with T,
          then that entry is running again, no new entry is created,
          and the open otherwise completes as in SLICE-2-1.

      - id: SLICE-2-7
        title: Same Slice Timer Stopped
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice open is run with ticket T,
          then T's entry for today is running, restarted if it exists and
          started otherwise,
          the ticket, branch, worktree, and manifest are unchanged,
          it reports that the slice was already open and its timer
          restarted, and it exits zero.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-2-INV-1
        title: At Most One Running Timer
        status: active
        description: >
          For every starting state and every outcome of slice open,
          at most one Harvest timer is running afterward.

      - id: SLICE-2-INV-2
        title: Failed Open Leaves No Trace
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run of slice open that exits non-zero, no time entry it
          created still exists, every entry that existed before is still
          there and running or stopped as it was, no branch or worktree it
          created still exists, every branch and worktree that existed
          before still does, no manifest exists for the slice, and the
          ticket's status is what it was before the run.

  - id: SLICE-3
    title: Slice Pause
    description: >
      Running slice pause stops the active slice's timer when you switch
      away, leaving the slice, its ticket, branch, worktree, and manifest
      as they are so it can be resumed later.
    status: active
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-02
    rationale: >
      Pausing through slice rather than hv keeps the timer owned by the
      slice, so a later resume restarts the same entry and the one-timer
      rule holds. Pausing is the command run most often, so it must be
      idempotent and refuse rather than guess when state is inconsistent.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Pausing automatically when a session ends
      - Slack focus status
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-3-1
        title: Pause Running Slice
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice whose timer is running,
          when slice pause is run,
          then the timer is stopped, the slice is still active, the ticket,
          branch, worktree, and manifest are unchanged, and it exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-3-2
        title: Already Paused
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice pause is run,
          then it reports that the slice is already paused, changes nothing,
          and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-3-3
        title: Nothing To Pause
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice,
          when slice pause is run,
          then it prints a single line saying no slice is active, changes
          nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-3-4
        title: Pause Mismatch
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice and a running Harvest timer for a different
          ticket or for no ticket,
          when slice pause is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-3-INV-1
        title: Pause Never Starts Or Deletes
        status: active
        description: >
          For every starting state, slice pause starts no timer, deletes no
          time entry, and leaves the ticket, local slice state, and manifest
          unchanged.

  - id: SLICE-4
    title: Slice Resume
    description: >
      Running slice resume restarts the paused active slice's timer, without
      needing the ticket number.
    status: active
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-02
    rationale: >
      SLICE-2-7 already resumes a paused slice when it is opened again by
      ticket number. Resume is the same operation addressed to whatever slice
      is active, which is what you want after a break without having to
      remember the ticket.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Resuming a slice other than the active one
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-4-1
        title: Resume Paused Slice
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice resume is run,
          then the slice ticket's entry for today is running, restarted if
          it exists and started otherwise, the ticket, branch, worktree, and
          manifest are unchanged, and it exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-4-2
        title: Already Running
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice whose timer is running,
          when slice resume is run,
          then it reports that the slice is already running, changes nothing,
          and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-4-3
        title: Nothing To Resume
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice,
          when slice resume is run,
          then it prints a single line saying no slice is active, changes
          nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-4-4
        title: Resume Mismatch
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice and a running Harvest timer for a different
          ticket or for no ticket,
          when slice resume is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-4-INV-1
        title: Resume Keeps One Timer
        status: active
        description: >
          For every starting state and every outcome of slice resume, at most
          one Harvest timer is running afterward, and no time entry is
          deleted.

  - id: SLICE-5
    title: Slice Close
    description: >
      Running slice close ends the active slice: its timer is stopped, the
      ticket moves to review (or done), the manifest is marked closed, and
      no slice is active afterward. The
      branch and worktree are left for review and merge.
    status: active
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-02
    rationale: >
      Close is the last housekeeping step of the lifecycle. Merging stays
      a human action, so close only records that the work is ready and
      frees the one-active-slice slot. Close posts no comment: slice ids are
      internal, and there is nothing yet worth telling the ticket's readers
      that the status change does not. Every step can therefore be undone.
      Default statuses, overridable in config: review is "dev complete" in
      ClickUp and "Waiting for review" in monday; done is "complete" in
      ClickUp and "Done" in monday.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Merging, pushing, or opening a merge request
      - Removing the branch or worktree
      - Logging decisions
      - Commenting on the ticket
      - Closing a slice that is not the active one
      - Slack focus status
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-5-1
        title: Close To Review
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T,
          when slice close is run,
          then the slice's timer is not running, T is in its configured
          review status, the manifest's status is closed, no slice is active,
          the branch and worktree still exist, and it exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-5-2
        title: Close To Done
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T,
          when slice close is run with --done,
          then it completes as in SLICE-5-1 except that T is in its
          configured done status.

      - id: SLICE-5-3
        title: Close Paused Slice
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice close is run,
          then it completes as in SLICE-5-1 without starting or stopping
          any timer.

      - id: SLICE-5-4
        title: Nothing To Close
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice,
          when slice close is run,
          then it prints a single line saying no slice is active, changes
          nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-5-5
        title: Close Mismatch
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice and a running Harvest timer for a different
          ticket or for no ticket,
          when slice close is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-5-6
        title: Close Partial Failure
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a step of slice close fails after an earlier step succeeded,
          when slice close is run,
          then it undoes the earlier steps it performed in reverse order,
          including restarting a timer it stopped, reports which step
          failed, and exits non-zero.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-5-INV-1
        title: Failed Close Leaves No Trace
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run of slice close that exits non-zero, the slice is
          still active, its timer's running state, the ticket's status, and
          the manifest are what they were before the run.

  - id: SLICE-6
    title: Slice Abandon
    description: >
      Running slice abandon ends the active slice without moving its
      ticket: its timer is stopped, the manifest is marked abandoned, and no
      slice is active afterward. The ticket's status, the Harvest time
      already logged, and the branch and worktree are all left as they are.
    status: active
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-03
    rationale: >
      Close is the only way to end a slice, and it always moves the ticket
      to review or done. Work that stops for any other reason, such as a
      ticket that turns out to be fixed already or a product being retired,
      needs a way to free the one-active-slice slot without claiming the
      work is ready. The time was really spent, so the Harvest entry stays.
      What happens to the ticket is left to a person. Like close, every
      step can be undone.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Changing, commenting on, or reassigning the ticket
      - Deleting or editing Harvest time
      - Removing the branch or worktree
      - Abandoning a slice that is not the active one
      - Recording a reason for abandoning
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-6-1
        title: Abandon
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T with its timer running,
          when slice abandon is run,
          then the timer is not running and its Harvest entry still exists,
          T's status is unchanged and was not written, the manifest's status
          is abandoned, no slice is active, the branch and worktree still
          exist, and it exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-6-2
        title: Abandon Paused Slice
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice abandon is run,
          then it completes as in SLICE-6-1 without starting or stopping
          any timer.

      - id: SLICE-6-3
        title: Nothing To Abandon
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice,
          when slice abandon is run,
          then it prints a single line saying no slice is active, changes
          nothing, and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-6-4
        title: Abandon Mismatch
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice and a running Harvest timer for a different
          ticket or for no ticket,
          when slice abandon is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-6-5
        title: Abandon Partial Failure
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a step of slice abandon fails after an earlier step succeeded,
          when slice abandon is run,
          then it undoes the earlier steps it performed in reverse order,
          including restarting a timer it stopped, reports which step
          failed, and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-6-6
        title: Reopen After Abandon
        status: active
        description: >
          Given ticket T's slice was abandoned,
          when slice open T is run,
          then a new slice for T opens on T's existing branch and worktree,
          with the next slice id.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-6-INV-1
        title: Abandon Never Touches The Ticket
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run of slice abandon, successful or not, no ticket
          status is written, and when it exits non-zero the slice is still
          active and its timer's running state and manifest are what they
          were before the run.

  - id: SLICE-7
    title: Abandon Reason
    description: >
      slice abandon --reason "<text>" records why a slice was abandoned in
      its manifest and reports it. The reason is optional: without it,
      abandon works exactly as before and the manifest records no reason.
    status: active
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-04
    rationale: >
      An abandoned manifest says that the work stopped but not why, and the
      why is what a later look back, or an orchestrator deciding whether to
      retry, needs. The reason stays in local state: SLICE-6 leaves the
      ticket to a person, and a reason posted to the ticket would undo that.
      It's optional so abandoning in a hurry stays one command. Manifests
      written before this change must still read back.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Posting the reason to the ticket or to Harvest
      - Requiring a reason
      - Reasons for close, pause or resume
      - Editing the reason after the slice is abandoned
      - Listing or searching past reasons
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-7-1
        title: Reason Recorded
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T,
          when slice abandon --reason "  fixed by ENG-14800  " is run,
          then it completes as in SLICE-6-1, the manifest's abandon reason
          is "fixed by ENG-14800" with the surrounding whitespace removed,
          the printed line includes the reason, and with --json the output
          has a reason field holding it.

      - id: SLICE-7-2
        title: No Reason
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice,
          when slice abandon is run without --reason,
          then it completes as in SLICE-6-1, the manifest records no
          reason, and with --json the reason field is null.

      - id: SLICE-7-3
        title: Empty Reason
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice,
          when slice abandon is run with --reason followed by an empty or
          all-whitespace value, or with --reason as the last argument,
          then it prints a usage error, changes nothing, and exits 2.

      - id: SLICE-7-4
        title: Reason Only On Abandon
        status: active
        description: >
          Given any command other than abandon,
          when it is run with --reason,
          then it prints a usage error, changes nothing, and exits 2.

      - id: SLICE-7-5
        title: Older Manifests
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a manifest written before this change, with no abandon
          reason line,
          when it is read,
          then it reads back with no reason and every other field as written.

      - id: SLICE-7-6
        title: Reason Round Trip
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a reason containing quotes, colons, a backslash, a newline
          and non-ASCII text,
          when the manifest is written and read back,
          then the reason is exactly what was written.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-7-INV-1
        title: Reason Stays Local
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run of slice abandon with a reason, successful or not,
          the reason is written only to the slice's manifest: never to the
          ticket, and never to a Harvest entry's notes.

  - id: SLICE-8
    title: Agent Run
    description: >
      slice run test|impl --task <file> --image <tag> runs one agent on the
      repository at HEAD in a Podman container that holds an export of
      HEAD, not the repository, in which only the role's own paths can be
      written. It writes the run's files to a new run directory and reads
      back the agent's report and patch. The repository is the current
      directory, or --repo. The role prompts and path globs come from the
      repository's .slice.toml; the Linux Spool binary and the token's env
      file come from slice's config.
    status: active
    interface: src/run.rs
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-06
    rationale: >
      Phase 1 and four slices since (INVARIANT-1, INVARIANT-2, TREE-1 and
      COVERAGE) ran the same manual steps every time: export, baseline,
      role files, a generated list of read-only mounts, the podman command,
      and reading the result. Doing them by hand is slow and easy to get
      subtly wrong, and the mounts are what keep each role to its own
      files. The repository at HEAD, rather than the active slice, is what
      a run needs, because most of that work had no ticket. The image is
      passed in, because each stack has its own build script, and building
      images is a separate concern. The prompts live in each repository,
      because what "done" means (the test, lint and format commands)
      differs per stack.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Building images or the Linux Spool binary
      - The network allow-list proxy
      - The churn guard and stream-json monitoring
      - slice verify, the test-hash lock, and recording the run in a
        slice manifest
      - Removing old run directories
      - Committing the patch (SLICE-9 stages it; a person commits)
      - Retrying a failed or blocked run
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-8-1
        title: Run Usage Errors
        status: active
        description: >
          Given slice run with no role, a role other than test or impl, no
          --task, no --image, a --task file that can't be read, or a flag
          run doesn't take,
          when it is run,
          then it prints a usage error naming the problem, starts no
          container, creates no run directory, and exits 2.

      - id: SLICE-8-2
        title: Repository Must Be Clean
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a repository with staged or unstaged changes to tracked
          files, or a path that isn't a git repository,
          when slice run is run on it,
          then it says so, starts no container, creates no run directory,
          and exits 1. Untracked files don't count as changes.

      - id: SLICE-8-3
        title: Setup Must Be Complete
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a repository with no .slice.toml, a .slice.toml with no
          path globs for the role (test for test, source for impl), a role
          prompt file that doesn't exist at HEAD, or a slice config with
          no Spool binary path or a path that doesn't exist,
          when slice run is run on it,
          then it names what's missing, starts no container, creates no run
          directory, and exits 1.

      - id: SLICE-8-4
        title: Configuration
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a .slice.toml with
          [paths] test = [globs] and source = [globs], and optionally
          [agent] test_prompt, impl_prompt, test_model, impl_model and
          timeout_secs; and a slice config with [agents] spool = <path>
          and optionally env_file = <path>,
          when slice run is run,
          then the prompt paths default to .slice/test-agent.md and
          .slice/impl-agent.md, the models to opus and sonnet, the timeout
          to 2700 seconds, and the env file to ~/.config/slice/agent.env.
          An unknown key in either file is an error naming it, and exits 1.

      - id: SLICE-8-5
        title: Write Sets
        status: active
        description: >
          Given the globs in .slice.toml, where ** matches any number of
          whole path segments, * matches any run of characters within one
          segment, and everything else matches itself,
          when a role's write set is decided,
          then the test role may write paths matching a test glob, and the
          impl role may write paths matching a source glob and no test
          glob. For example, with test = ["**/*_test.go"] and
          source = ["**/*.go"], a.go and pkg/b.go are impl paths and
          pkg/b_test.go is a test path, and with test = ["tests/**"],
          tests/x.rs and tests/common/mod.rs are test paths and src/x.rs is
          not.

      - id: SLICE-8-6
        title: Workspace
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a clean repository,
          when slice run is run,
          then it creates a new run directory under
          $XDG_STATE_HOME/slice/runs (default ~/.local/state/slice/runs)
          whose name includes the role, holding a workspace with exactly
          the files tracked at HEAD and their contents, a baseline of that
          workspace in a git directory kept outside it, and a role
          directory holding prompt.md (the role's prompt file as at HEAD),
          task.md (the --task file) and report.schema.json (the report
          schema built into slice).

      - id: SLICE-8-7
        title: Container
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a run directory as in SLICE-8-6,
          when the container is started,
          then it uses the given image, the role's model and the timeout,
          passes the env file by path, mounts the workspace writable at
          /work, mounts read-only on top every file tracked at HEAD that
          isn't in the role's write set at /work/<path>, the role
          directory at /role, and the Spool binary at
          /usr/local/bin/spool, and runs claude with the task as the
          prompt, the role prompt appended to the system prompt, the
          report schema, bypassed permissions, no setting sources, a
          strict MCP config and no session persistence.

      - id: SLICE-8-8
        title: Report Read
        status: active
        description: >
          Given the container exits with JSON output whose
          structured_output is a report (status green or blocked,
          files_touched, assumptions, questions, summary),
          when the run finishes,
          then the report, the cost, the duration and the turn count are
          read from it, the output is kept as result.json and the
          container's stderr as agent.log in the run directory, and the
          patch is the workspace's diff against its baseline, new files
          included, kept as changes.patch in the run directory.

      - id: SLICE-8-9
        title: Run Failed
        status: active
        description: >
          Given the container can't start, exits non-zero, times out, or
          exits without output holding a valid report,
          when the run finishes,
          then slice run says the run failed and why, names the run
          directory and its agent.log, stages nothing, and exits 1.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-8-INV-1
        title: The Container Never Sees The Repository
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run, every path mounted into the container is inside
          the run directory, except the Spool binary, mounted read-only,
          and the env file, which is passed by path and never read, copied
          or printed by slice.

  - id: SLICE-9
    title: Patch Staging
    description: >
      After an agent run, slice run checks every path the patch touches
      against the role's write set. A green report with a patch that
      passes is staged in the repository with git apply --index and never
      committed. Anything else stages nothing.
    status: active
    interface: src/run.rs
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-06
    rationale: >
      The read-only mounts stop an agent changing a tracked file it
      mustn't, but not creating a new one, for example a source file from
      the test role, so the path check is what keeps the source/test split
      complete. Staging rather than committing keeps a person between
      every agent and the history: the staged diff is what gets reviewed,
      and the commit follows approval, as in every slice so far. A blocked
      report means the spec needs work, so its patch is kept for reading
      but not staged.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Committing, amending or pushing
      - Applying a patch from an earlier run
      - Checks beyond the path check (tests, lint, coverage; that's
        slice verify)
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-9-1
        title: Green Patch Staged
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a run whose report is green and whose patch touches only
          paths in the role's write set,
          when the run finishes,
          then the patch is applied to the repository's working tree and
          index, new files included, nothing is committed, and slice run
          prints the report's status, summary, assumptions and files, the
          cost, the duration and the run directory, and exits 0.

      - id: SLICE-9-2
        title: Path Outside The Write Set
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a run whose patch adds, changes, deletes or renames any
          path outside the role's write set,
          when the run finishes,
          then nothing is staged, slice run lists every such path, keeps
          the patch in the run directory, and exits 1, whatever the
          report's status.

      - id: SLICE-9-3
        title: Blocked
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a run whose report is blocked,
          when the run finishes,
          then nothing is staged, slice run prints the report's questions,
          assumptions and summary, keeps the patch in the run directory,
          and exits 1.

      - id: SLICE-9-4
        title: Repository Moved
        status: active
        description: >
          Given HEAD changed, or tracked files were changed, while the
          agent ran, or the patch otherwise doesn't apply,
          when the run finishes,
          then nothing is staged, slice run says why, keeps the patch in
          the run directory, and exits 1.

      - id: SLICE-9-5
        title: JSON Output
        status: active
        description: >
          Given --json,
          when slice run finishes after a container ran,
          then it prints one JSON object with "outcome" ("staged",
          "rejected", "blocked", "moved" or "failed"), "run_dir",
          "report" (the agent's report, or null when the run failed),
          "rejected_paths" ([] unless rejected), "cost_usd",
          "duration_ms" and "turns" (null when unknown), and exits as
          without --json.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-9-INV-1
        title: Only The Write Set Is Staged
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run, successful or not, slice run never commits,
          never moves HEAD or a branch, and never stages a path outside
          the role's write set; when it exits non-zero, the repository's
          index and working tree are as they were before the run.
